 ## Records to keep
+- For the custom probe's independent CT cross-check, record measured R39 and effective C42 capacitance, measurement conditions and uncertainty, plus the complete CT/acquisition gain and phase. C42's specified GRM31C5C1H104JA01L is 100 nF C0G ±5%; nominal 100 nF is not a calibration value. The nominal 3 Ω / 100 nF burden alone gives −6.4526° and −0.6335% amplitude at 60 kHz. Correct with the measured complex transfer before integrating current; do not treat a capacitance-meter reading through the intact parallel 3 Ω burden as an isolated capacitor measurement. This does not change the commissioned current limits or CT_ZC calibration.
 - Photos of both boards before first power, including the shim and pad selected for each FET (bench-sink §6.2).
 - The coil traveller: M1–M5 per coil, plus M4 for every pan you will cook on. Send them back to the coil study for its model
